# Copyright Image Scanner — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in values as needed:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# No variables are required for basic functionality — the Wikimedia Commons
# provider (free, no key) is always available and is the only one enabled by
# default. All keys below are optional: they make additional reverse image
# search providers selectable in the picker, but each stays OFF until you
# check it for a scan.
# Restart the dev server after changing this file.

# ── Google Lens (SerpAPI) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables the "serpapi" provider: web-wide reverse image search by the
# image's public URL (~250 free searches/month, then paid).
# Get a key: https://serpapi.com/dashboard
# SERPAPI_API_KEY=your-serpapi-key

# ── Google Cloud Vision ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables the "google-vision" provider: official Web Detection; uploads the
# image bytes directly (1,000 free units/month, then paid). Requires the
# Vision API to be enabled and billing configured on the GCP project.
# GOOGLE_VISION_API_KEY=your-vision-api-key

# ── Custom reverse-search endpoint ──────────────────────────────────────
# Enables the "custom" provider: your own HTTP endpoint (bring your own key).
# The URL may contain {sha1} / {sha256} placeholders, substituted per image.
# The endpoint receives { sha1, sha256, mimeType } and should return JSON
# matches: [{ "sourceName": "...", "sourceUrl": "https://...", "similarity": 95 }]
# REVERSE_SEARCH_CUSTOM_URL=https://your-endpoint.example/lookup/{sha256}
# REVERSE_SEARCH_CUSTOM_API_KEY=your-key
# Header used to send the API key (default: Authorization)
# REVERSE_SEARCH_CUSTOM_AUTH_HEADER=X-Api-Key
